# Use existing terminology

Before adding a method, field, or variable name, search this repo for the same idea. Use a word that already means that thing.

## Use words already here

- `trimToNull` / `trimmed` — blank becomes null (`StringUtils.trimToNull`)
- `parse` — read a raw value into a known value (`parseClaims`, `fromJson`)
- `normalize` — trim text and collapse whitespace, and return a string (`TtsTextUtil.normalize`, `InterpretationService.normalize`)
- `sanitize` — make one string safe for its storage key (`sanitizeSlug`)
- The field's own name when the value is that field: `request`, `channel`, `contact`, `email`, `message`

## Do not

- Invent a new metaphor for an idea that already has a word (`oneLine`, `resolved`, `contactChannel` when the field is `channel`)
- Call a different job `normalize`. In this repo `normalize` does not reject a request and does not return null

```java
// ❌ new metaphor; normalize in this repo does not reject a request
request = normalize(request);
var contact = oneLine(request.contact());

// ✅ same words the repo already uses
var contact = StringUtils.trimToNull(request.contact());
var channel = parseChannel(request.channel());
```
